            <ArticleTitle>Bombesin-Like Receptor 3: Physiology of a Functional Orphan.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>603-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.tem.2016.03.003</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1043-2760(16)00037-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bombesin-like receptor 3 (BRS-3) is an X-linked orphan Gq-coupled receptor that regulates food intake, metabolic rate, body temperature, heart rate, blood pressure, and insulin secretion. Most BRS-3 actions occur via the brain, through mechanisms including regulating sympathetic outflow. Ablation of Brs3 causes obesity, while synthetic agonists produce weight loss.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Published by Elsevier Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
